  "body": "First slice of the plasma work (#621 research → #669-#672): a **`plasma` machine kind** and the **Tormach 1300PL**.\n\n## What changed\n- **`Kind::Plasma`** (`kind: plasma`, \"plasma cutting\"), declared only and never inferred from the axes. `Kind` moves to `crates/post/src/machine/kind.rs` and is re-exported.\n- **File rules,** in one place: `machine/plasma.rs::plasma_refusals`. These are refused by name:\n  - any `spindle.*` key, each one separately;\n  - `live_tool`;\n  - coolant (station or tooling root);\n  - any rotary axis.\n  - The Machines-pane validator also requires X, Y and Z (Z is the torch lifter).\n  - The rules are held at every door: `parse_mch`, the validator, and `Machine::is_sane` for project files and `SetSetupMachine`.\n- **Machine check** (`crates/app/src/machine/plasma.rs`):\n  - **Judged:** X/Y travel (arc quarter points included), the X/Y share of each feed, and the tool count.\n  - **Refused by name:** a non-plasma op (\"a Face operation is milling work - a plasma table cuts only plasma operations\"), a tool with rpm, and a tilted move.\n  - **Skipped:** Z depth and travel, and rpm and spindle power. They are **named, not failed**: a new non-blocking `MachineCheck.notes`, which the status line prints as \"not judged: …\".\n  - The per-move helpers move to `machine/judge.rs`, so `mod.rs` drops from 427 to 370 lines.\n- **Command door:** `family_gate` refuses milling and turning ops on a plasma setup, and the ribbon shows no section. **No op can be posted on a plasma table until #670.**\n- **Posts:** a new `posting::PLASMA_POSTS`, empty until #671. Every cutting post declines a plasma table, and `post_offer` never offers a post that wouldn't serve the mounted machine.\n- **`assets/machines/tormach-1300pl.mch`** (UM10720 v1223A §2.2.1 and the 03/24 spec sheet):\n  - inch; X ±48.5, Y ±50, Z ±3.9. The smaller of the two documents' figures (the manual says X 50 / Y 51.5); both are recorded;\n  - 1000 IPM on X/Y and 120 IPM on Z; rapid unstated;\n  - a torch head with no spindle; `number_of_tools: 1`; no `safe_retract` (the plasma post retracts with G30).\n- **UI:** the machine editor's kind combo and the Machines pane's New blank list offer plasma.\n- **Docs:** `assets/machines/AGENTS.md`.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/669-plasma-kind.md`.\n  - Kerf lives on the torch tool, as its diameter, so the existing offset code works unchanged.\n  - Coolant is refused.\n  - A second tool, such as a scribe, stays allowed.\n\n**Seams left for the sibling issues:**\n- **#670:** add a `Family` arm in the exhaustive `cuts_plasma`, plus a torch tool kind (relax `Tool::is_sane`'s rpm > 0 for torches only).\n- **#671:** add a BUILTINS entry and its name to `PLASMA_POSTS`.\n- **#672:** owns what the check skips.\n\n## How tested\n- **New `plasma_machine` (6):**\n  - spindle, coolant and rotary keys and a missing Z are refused by name;\n  - an unknown kind is still refused, and undeclared XYZ reads as a mill;\n  - the 1300PL spec pin;\n  - the check skips depth and rpm with a note and judges XY (a mill-kind copy does report Z);\n  - a mill op is refused at the command door and at the verification gate;\n  - a 1300PL setup round-trips byte-identical, and a hand-edited rpm refuses to load.\n- **Updated:** the machine, machine_library, machine_edit and tormach_safe_retract expectations.\n- **Gate:**\n  - machine, machine_edit, machine_library, tormach_machines, tormach_safe_retract, sinumerik_safe_retract, axis_direction, posting, conformance, project_roundtrip, ribbon, lathe_post, setup_mounts_post, tormach_post, vmc_stroke and lathe_stroke pass;\n  - camcraft-post passes, and the ui machine and ribbon lib tests pass;\n  - clippy is clean on post, app and ui.\n\n**MACHINES list:** this PR appends to `posting::MACHINES`, as do #624, #627, #634 and #654. Whichever merges later takes a trivial list merge.\n\nChangelog: A plasma machine kind (`kind: plasma` - X/Y cut, Z torch lifter, no spindle; spindle, coolant and rotary keys refused by name; machine check judges X/Y travel and feed, skips Z depth and rpm with a named note) and the Tormach 1300PL machine (UM10720 / spec sheet 03/24); no op or post serves it yet (#670, #671) (#669)\n\nFixes #669\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
